<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Free website audit</nav>
    <h1>Is your website costing you customers?</h1>
    <p class="lede">A free, honestly reviewed look at your website's design, mobile experience, loading speed and ability to turn visitors into enquiries — built for home improvement businesses.</p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="#audit-form" data-track-cta="website_audit">Get my free website audit</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="problems-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="problems-h">Common problems we find on contractor websites</h2>
      <p class="lede">Most of these cost a business enquiries every single day, quietly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>Slow to load on a phone</h3><p>Most of your visitors are searching on their phone, mid-job or in a driveway. A slow page loses them before they see what you do.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>No clear next step</h3><p>A visitor who can't find the phone number or a quote button in a few seconds goes back to Google and calls someone else.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Nothing that proves you're legitimate</h3><p>No licence number, no service area, no real photos of finished work — nothing that answers "can I trust this business?"</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Built for desktop, not the phone it's actually viewed on</h3><p>Text that's too small, buttons too close together, menus that don't work with a thumb.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="includes-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="includes-h">What the audit covers</h2>
      <p class="lede">Ten categories, every time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>Website design</h3><p>First impression, visual hierarchy and whether it looks like the established, trusted choice in your area.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Mobile usability</h3><p>How it actually behaves on a phone, not just whether it "resizes."</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Page loading performance</h3><p>Measured with Google PageSpeed Insights where your site can be tested.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>On-page SEO</h3><p>Whether your titles, headings and copy are written for what people actually search.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Calls to action</h3><p>Whether it's obvious what to do next, and how many times you ask.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Contact form usability</h3><p>How many fields, how much friction, and whether it works on mobile.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Business credibility</h3><p>Licensing, insurance, service area and real project photos — or the lack of them.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Navigation</h3><p>Whether someone can find your services and service area in two clicks or fewer.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Accessibility</h3><p>Colour contrast, readable text size and whether a keyboard can reach every link.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Conversion opportunities</h3><p>The specific changes we'd make first, and why, in order of expected impact.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="method-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 id="method-h">How we score it</h2>
      <p class="lede">We separate what's measured from what's judged, so you know which is which.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="rows">
      <div class="row"><h3>Measured</h3><p>Page loading performance comes from Google's own PageSpeed Insights tool, where your website can be tested by it. If it can't be tested (some site builders block it), we say so instead of guessing.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Manually reviewed</h3><p>Design, mobile usability, credibility, navigation, accessibility and conversion opportunities are reviewed by a person on our team against the same ten categories every time.</p></div>
      <div class="row"><h3>Not assessed</h3><p>If something can't be measured or confidently reviewed from what's public on your site, we mark it "not assessed" rather than invent a number.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head"><h2 id="faq-h">Questions before you request yours</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details><summary>Is the audit really free?</summary><div><p>Yes. There's no cost and no obligation to buy anything afterward.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Is this an automated score or a real review?</summary><div><p>Both, where possible. We check real, measurable signals like page speed through Google's own PageSpeed Insights tool, and a person on our team reviews design, mobile experience, credibility and calls to action by hand — we don't generate a score from nothing.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>What do I get?</summary><div><p>A short written summary of what's working, what's likely costing you enquiries, and what we'd prioritize first — delivered by email, with an offer to walk through it on a call.</p></div></details>
      <details><summary>Do I have to switch to WebConvertPro?</summary><div><p>No. The audit is yours either way. If you'd like help acting on it, we'll explain your options, including our free website preview.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--ink" id="audit-form">
  <div class="wrap lead">
    <div class="lead-copy">
      <h2>Get my free website audit</h2>
      <p class="lede">Tell us where to look. We'll reply by email with what we found.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Real PageSpeed data where your site supports it</li>
        <li>A person reviews the rest — no fabricated score</li>
        <li>No payment details, no obligation</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
